+MFEM compiled with CUDA
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+
+When ``MFEM`` is compiled with ``CUDA``, the sources containing kernels
+of ``MFEM`` (``mfem::forall``) must be compiled by ``nvcc``. The CMake
+module ``MFEMMGISDeviceCode.cmake``, installed with ``mfem-mgis`` and
+loaded by ``find_package(MFEMMGIS)``, provides:
+
+- ``mfem_mgis_enable_device_language()``, to be called at file scope
+  (not in a function), which enables the ``CUDA`` language with the
+  compilers used to build ``MFEM`` (unless ``CMAKE_CUDA_COMPILER`` and
+  ``CMAKE_CUDA_HOST_COMPILER`` are given);
+- ``mfem_mgis_compile_as_device_code(target sources...)``, which compiles
+  the given sources of the target as ``CUDA`` code, for the GPU
+  architectures of ``MFEM``.
+
+Both do nothing when ``MFEM`` is not compiled with ``CUDA``. CMake 3.18
+or later is then required. ``MFEM`` compiled with ``HIP`` is not
+supported yet. The tests which require a GPU are disabled by
+``-Denable-gpu-tests=OFF``.
+
 Creating a simple example based on ``mfem-mgis``
 ------------------------------------------------
 
diff --git a/src/MFEMMGISConfig.cmake.in b/src/MFEMMGISConfig.cmake.in
index 9a38c60160..487ac2e67a 100644
--- a/src/MFEMMGISConfig.cmake.in
+++ b/src/MFEMMGISConfig.cmake.in
@@ -46,8 +46,6 @@ if(NOT _mfem_mgis_mfem_described)
                "@MFEM_MGIS_MFEM_CUDA_HOST_COMPILER@")
   set_property(GLOBAL PROPERTY MFEM_MGIS_MFEM_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES
                "@MFEM_MGIS_MFEM_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES@")
-  set_property(GLOBAL PROPERTY MFEM_MGIS_MFEM_CXX_STANDARD
-               "@MFEM_MGIS_MFEM_CXX_STANDARD@")
 endif()
 
 # Require MGIS
diff --git a/tests/CMakeLists.txt b/tests/CMakeLists.txt
index 700de80173..154e1298db 100644
--- a/tests/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/tests/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -786,20 +786,23 @@ if(MFEM_USE_MPI)
 endif(MFEM_USE_MPI)
 
 # DeviceForallTest executable: a kernel of MFEM, compiled as CUDA code
-# when MFEM is compiled with CUDA. The test on the GPU requires one.
-add_test_executable(DeviceForallTest)
-mfem_mgis_compile_as_device_code(DeviceForallTest DeviceForallTest.cxx)
-add_test(NAME DeviceForallTest-cpu
-         COMMAND DeviceForallTest --expected cpu)
-if((MFEM_USE_CUDA STREQUAL "YES") AND enable-gpu-tests)
-  add_test(NAME DeviceForallTest-cuda
-           COMMAND DeviceForallTest --device cuda --expected cuda)
-  # the processes of a node use its GPUs in turn
-  if(MFEM_USE_MPI)
-    add_test(NAME DeviceForallTestP-cuda
-             COMMAND mpirun -n 2 ./DeviceForallTest --device cuda
-                     --expected cuda)
-  endif(MFEM_USE_MPI)
+# when MFEM is compiled with CUDA (not supported yet with HIP). The test on
+# the GPU requires one.
+if(NOT MFEM_USE_HIP STREQUAL "YES")
+  add_test_executable(DeviceForallTest)
+  mfem_mgis_compile_as_device_code(DeviceForallTest DeviceForallTest.cxx)
+  add_test(NAME DeviceForallTest-cpu
+           COMMAND DeviceForallTest --expected cpu)
+  if((MFEM_USE_CUDA STREQUAL "YES") AND enable-gpu-tests)
+    add_test(NAME DeviceForallTest-cuda
+             COMMAND DeviceForallTest --device cuda --expected cuda)
+    # the processes of a node use its GPUs in turn
+    if(MFEM_USE_MPI)
+      add_test(NAME DeviceForallTestP-cuda
+               COMMAND mpirun -n 2 ./DeviceForallTest --device cuda
+                       --expected cuda)
+    endif(MFEM_USE_MPI)
+  endif()
 endif()
 
